@sokra I think there is still a problem here. 

`System.import()` used dynamically this way does not work for me if I try to import a module that has an `export default`. However, it works with a classic `modules.export`:
e.g.

```
var CollectionModel = AccessControlledModel.extend({
    resourceName: 'collection'
});
export default CollectionModel;
```

fails to be imported correctly with `System.import`.
However this work:

```
var CollectionModel = AccessControlledModel.extend({
    resourceName: 'collection'
});
module.exports = CollectionModel;
```

I noticed that the test you added in [issue-2443](https://github.com/webpack/webpack/tree/93f38132d118e19337dee3c091364902cf15f499/test/cases/chunks/issue-2443) imports 3 files, and they _all_ use `module.exports`, not ES6 `export default`.

Maybe I'm misunderstanding `System.import`, but since it's introduced in the [ES6 Modules](https://gist.github.com/sokra/27b24881210b56bbaff7#es6-modules) section of "[What's new in webpack 2](https://gist.github.com/sokra/27b24881210b56bbaff7)", I assumed it would be able to handle `export default`, the same way `import... from...` does. I want to be able to import `CollectionModel` with `import...from`, as well as `System.import` (using a directory + pattern), but it seems I would have to provide _both_ `export default` _and_ `module.exports` in the same file?

Thanks

